{"is_source_file": true, "format": "C++ header file", "description": "This file defines a template class ScopeGuard, which ensures that a specified functor is executed when a scope is exited. It provides mechanisms to create, move, and disable scope guards, preventing resource leaks or ensuring cleanup tasks are performed. Additionally, it includes a helper function to create scope guards conveniently.", "external_files": ["<utility>"], "external_methods": ["std::move", "std::forward"], "published": ["android::base::ScopeGuard", "android::base::make_scope_guard"], "classes": [{"name": "ScopeGuard", "description": "A template class that accepts a callable object and guarantees its execution upon scope exit unless disabled."}], "methods": [{"name": "ScopeGuard(F && f)", "description": "Constructor that takes a functor and starts managing it. Marked constexpr for compile-time evaluation and noexcept for exception safety.", "scope": "android::base::ScopeGuard", "scopeKind": "class"}, {"name": "ScopeGuard(ScopeGuard&& that)", "description": "Move constructor transferring ownership of the functor and active state from another ScopeGuard."}, {"name": "ScopeGuard<Functor>(ScopeGuard<Functor>&& that)", "description": "Templated move constructor allowing move semantics from another ScopeGuard with a different but compatible functor type."}, {"name": "~ScopeGuard()", "description": "Destructor that calls the stored functor if still active, ensuring execution on scope exit.", "scope": "android::base::ScopeGuard", "scopeKind": "class"}, {"name": "void Disable()", "description": "Method to deactivate the scope guard, preventing the functor from executing.", "scope": "android::base::ScopeGuard", "scopeKind": "class"}, {"name": "bool active() const", "description": "Returns whether the scope guard is still active (i.e., will execute the functor).", "scope": "android::base::ScopeGuard", "scopeKind": "class"}, {"name": "ScopeGuard(ScopeGuard && that)", "scope": "android::base::ScopeG